{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772838597,"nonce":"MfUqnUy4zQp1VQ3SOdxVfZu/j1w=","title":"Dashboard: single-file diffs should still show filename pill","message":"## Problem\nWhen an auth request card has changes to only one file, the diff viewer shows the diff content directly without any filename indicator. When multiple files are changed, there are clickable pills/tabs showing each filename. The single-file case should still show the filename pill for consistency and clarity.\n\n## Expected Behavior\nEven with a single changed file, display the filename pill above the diff. The user should always be able to see which file they are looking at without having to infer it from the diff content.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e","files":null}]}